# clrsrc .gitignore — ALLOWLIST strategy.
#
# The working directory contains tens of GB of training data, logs, binaries,
# third-party engines, cluster-management scripts with hard-coded hosts, and
# personal notes. To avoid ever leaking any of that, we ignore EVERYTHING by
# default and then explicitly re-include only the curated set that makes up the
# published project.

# 1. Ignore everything in the repo root.
/*

# 2. Re-include the curated release set.
!/.gitignore
!/.cargo/
!/Cargo.toml
!/Cargo.lock
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/CREDITS.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/CLUSTER.md
!/EMBEDDED.md
!/NNUE_FORMAT.md
!/src/
!/tests/
!/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md
!/tools/
!/hooks/

# 3. Safety nets inside the re-included directories.
#    (Nothing build- or cache-related should ever be committed.)
**/target/
**/__pycache__/
*.rs.bk
*.tmp

# 4. Never commit large binary artifacts — they are published as Release assets.
*.nnue
*.bin
*.exe
*.pgn
